# eConsult window monitor — environment
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in, or (preferred) mount this path from a 1Password
# Environment: Desktop app → Environments → Destinations → "Local .env file".
# 1Password streams the values through a FIFO, so nothing is written to disk.
# https://www.1password.dev/environments/local-env-file
#
# Not a secret as such — but it names a particular surgery, and this repo is
# public, so it is kept out of the source tree along with everything in data/.
#
# Read under a short deadline: if 1Password is locked (as it may well be when
# launchd starts the daemon at boot) the monitor falls back to a one-line
# `target_url.local` at the repo root rather than blocking.

ECONSULT_BASE_URL=https://your-surgery.example.com
